Feature: EN 1991 structural scene
  The actions snapshot and its check report project to a deterministic, locale-free 3D scene, a set of 2D diagrams and drag handles.

  Further specification assertions, asserted by the Rust unit tests of the crate and not by the platform adapters:
  - wind zones partition the walls and the roof: Given the duo-pitch building of 25 m by 15 m and 20 m height When the scene is projected Then the wind zones A to J are pressure glyphs and each carries q_p times the tabulated c_pe,10 And the zones of both side walls together cover the wall areas of the closed-form partition of EN 1991-1-4 Figure 7.5
  - both internal pressure cases get arrows: Given the building and a wind face in zone D When the scene is projected Then the arrows of c_pi = +0.2 and c_pi = -0.3 carry the net pressure q_p (c_pe - c_pi)
  - snow follows the roof geometry: Given a duo-pitch roof with a parapet and a drift obstruction When the scene is projected Then each slope carries mu_1 times s_k and the drifts carry the capped mu_2 over the drift length
  - failing rows are visible: Given a floor whose assumed imposed load is too small When the scene is projected Then the floor has error style, a diagonal hatch and a utilisation above 1
  - handles write document leaves: Given the building When the height handle is dragged by 2.04 m Then one write sets "height" to 22.0 m And the roof pitch handle writes degrees and the storey handle snaps to an integer
  - diagrams agree with the closed forms: Given the European annex document and its check report When the diagrams are built Then an independent Python oracle reproduces q_p(z), c_pe(A), mu_1, mu_2, mu_3, the standard, external and hydrocarbon fire curves, the influence line and the Janssen pressure by ODE integration
  - the fire and traffic tracks scrub time and tandem position: Given the European annex document with a nominal standard fire and a road bridge When the scene is projected Then the fire time track binds the gas temperature 20 + 345 log10(8 t + 1) at every keyframe And the traffic position track shows the LM1 tandem at one deck position per keyframe layer
  - The primary structure deflects under the characteristic wind and snow load: Given the default actions model with a valid wind zone and snow zone When the scene is projected Then a wind-loaded column drifts one five-hundredth of its height under the net wind line load and a snow-loaded roof beam sags one two-hundred-fiftieth of its span And both deflected shapes equal the closed-form beam lines of the mechanics kernel and play as a load ramp from zero to the characteristic load
  - the selected load group shows its alternative load model: Given a bridge with load group gr1b or gr4 When the scene is projected Then the LM2 axle or the LM4 crowd moves from the hidden alternatives layer to the visible traffic layer, and the default group gr1a keeps both hidden
  - the LM1 tandem travels along the lanes: Given a road bridge When the scene is projected Then the hidden overlay "bridge:travel" carries the mid-span moment of the tandem group of all loaded lanes at eleven stops and its envelope (an independent scipy and sympy oracle gives Q (L - s)/2 and the support reaction envelope), the track "traffic-travel" scrubs the stops and the diagram "bridge:travel" plots the influence-line envelope
  - wind zones are a pressure colour map: Given the building and its c_pe zones A to J When the scene is projected Then each zone glyph carries the fields net pressure for c_pi = +0.2, net pressure for c_pi = -0.3 and the external pressure, the larger magnitude active
  - roofs carry a snow load profile: Given a duo-pitch roof with a parapet and an obstruction When the scene is projected Then the sampled line "roof:profile" holds 13 samples of s = mu s_k C_e C_t along the section, raised by the drift triangles (an independent numpy and sympy oracle reproduces mu along a drift triangle)
  - The psi chart lists the combination factors of the floor categories, snow and wind: Given the default actions model When the diagrams are built Then the chart holds psi0, psi1 and psi2 per imposed-load category in use and for snow and wind with the values of EN 1990 Table A1.1 And each floor category marker is bound to the imposed-load check of its floor and the table twin lists every factor
  - every check outcome has a 3D owner: Given the demo documents and the full showcase When their checks are evaluated Then each check routes to the entity that draws its row, to the bridge deck, building, crane, silo, fire or thermal entity of its family, or to the global badge when it is a document-level family without a row, And the entity of a route stands in the scene, is the one the outcome focus selects and shows at least the severity of the worst check it owns
  - every numeric field has a viewport grip: Given the snapshot schema and the documents that populate every collection When the handles of all entities are collected Then each numeric row field and each numeric document scalar is written by a geometric grip or a gauge grip, except the placement height and rotation, And a gauge writes the current value at zero drag, moves it by twenty schema steps per metre, stays inside its physical range and its step equals the schema step
  - every check family is drawn: Given the check families of EN 1991 When a check is looked up by the longest prefix of its id Then its family has a dedicated diagram or is an outcome family, never both, And an entity owning checks of outcome families gets one diagram with a utilisation bar per check against the limit line at 1 and a table twin
